{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And he shall put upon it living water into a vessel</b> – The meaning is not that he should put the ashes into the vessel first and then put water upon the ashes, for thus our Sages taught (Sotah 16): one who puts ashes first and afterward the water is invalid. They derived this precisely from \"living water into a vessel\" — that their living quality must be in the vessel. And perhaps this is because it did not say, \"And they shall take for the unclean person from the ashes of the burnt-offering of purification into a vessel, and he shall put upon it living water,\" but rather its meaning is: and he shall put upon the ashes living water that were already in the vessel — to say that he should mix the ashes into the water that is in the vessel until the water covers them."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The parenthetical verse paraphrase beginning ולקחו לטמא is Ramban's own reconstruction of what the verse might have said had it intended the other order; it is not an actual verse citation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:52.737528788Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}